# LF in the repository AND in every working copy, whatever core.autocrlf says: a file copied into the
# APK must be byte-identical whether it was built on Windows or on Linux (lesson of Notes Tech, whose
# res/raw pages differed by one byte per line depending on the machine).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.rftvault binary
# The OCR's trained data (docs D-032): checked by SHA-256 before use, so never touched by a conversion.
*.traineddata binary
# The viewers' corpus: files as REAL software wrote them (CRLF, UTF-16, Windows-1252), byte for byte.
tools/corpus/*/** binary
